pdf: undo / redo forget cached resources for the objects they swap

The document caches the font, colorspace and image objects it added
(doc->resources), keyed by digest, so the next appearance reuses them.
pdf_undo / pdf_redo purged the object store but not these tables. An
undo that took away an object created in that step, e.g. the font of a
free text appearance, left the cache pointing at a missing object, and
the next free text appearance used it: the text drew in a fallback font
with the wrong glyphs (#6549). Undo / redo now drop table entries for
every object they swap.
---
diff --git a/include/mupdf/pdf/resource.h b/include/mupdf/pdf/resource.h
index 921338baee..bc62460102 100644
--- a/include/mupdf/pdf/resource.h
+++ b/include/mupdf/pdf/resource.h
@@ -88,6 +88,8 @@ pdf_obj *pdf_find_image_resource(fz_context *ctx, pdf_document *doc, fz_image *i
 pdf_obj *pdf_insert_image_resource(fz_context *ctx, pdf_document *doc, pdf_image_resource_key *key, pdf_obj *obj);
 void pdf_drop_resource_tables(fz_context *ctx, pdf_document *doc);
 void pdf_purge_local_resources(fz_context *ctx, pdf_document *doc);
+/* SumatraPDF: forget cached font / colorspace / image resources that are object num */
+void pdf_purge_resources_for_object(fz_context *ctx, pdf_document *doc, int num);
 
 typedef struct pdf_function pdf_function;
 
